invariant: INV-35
file: build.h
catches: test/lib-pair-check.sh
reason: build.h gives the QUIC transport's record the record transport's
  name, so two transports name their records alike again, as every
  object did before docs/decisions.md 61. A QUIC object then defines
  ch_build_record while PUBLIC names ch_build_quic: nmedit refuses to
  package it on macOS, and objcopy localizes it elsewhere, so the QUIC
  half of cocuyo's pair links against the record-mode object's record
  and ch_build_matches answers 0. test/lib-pair-check.sh objects either
  way.

--- old
#define ch_build ch_build_quic
--- new
#define ch_build ch_build_record
